## Boot context (recorded because the isolated stack is minimal)

- `init_permissions` one-shot ran first (chowns the storage named volume); api
  then generated its `.dify_secret_key` in storage and booted gunicorn on 5001.
- api reached health `healthy` after DB migration completed.
- web reached api:5001 during SSR (earlier 500s were the pre-migration api
  refusing connections; cleared once migration finished).

## Known limitation (honest)

Same-daemon simulation: all images already existed locally (Phase F build,
2026-08-11). `docker compose up --pull never` provably never attempted a pull
on this run, but this cannot prove a truly offline host; the equivalent proof
on a network-isolated Docker host remains NOT_RUN.
